# Trivy vulnerability ignore-list, read automatically from the repository
# root by `trivy fs .` and `trivy image`.
#
# TD-024 (see TECH_DEBT.md): rumqttc 0.25.1 (MQTT connector) hard-pins
# rustls-webpki = "^0.102.8", which carries these four advisories. The
# vulnerable code is unreachable from Arca: rumqttc only uses this copy of
# webpki for one error variant and never configures a CRL; MQTTS certificate
# validation actually runs through rustls 0.23.40 -> the already-patched
# rustls-webpki 0.103.13. No upstream fix exists yet. Re-assess if rumqttc
# ever starts configuring CRLs, or if a new rumqttc release relaxes the
# rustls-webpki requirement.
GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8
GHSA-pwjx-qhcg-rvj4
GHSA-xgp8-3hg3-c2mh
GHSA-965h-392x-2mh5

# TD-027 (see TECH_DEBT.md): Kubernetes manifest findings accepted on purpose.
#
# KSV-0125 "images only from trusted registries": the check's allow-list does
# not contain ghcr.io, which is where Arca publishes its images (the only
# official registry). Pinning to a different registry would mean not using the
# published images.
KSV-0125
# KSV-0013 "image tag :latest" in deploy/kubernetes/arca-cluster.yaml: `latest`
# is the evaluation default there, with a comment next to the image saying so
# and pointing at "Choosing a tag" in the Installation guide for production.
# (The console manifest pins the release tag and has no finding.)
KSV-0013
